**🎯 Functional Correctness** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**

**Trim the MathML `<ci>` name before you use it as the variable identity.**

The guard trims the value only for the emptiness check. The untrimmed value then keys `frame.node("free-variable", name)`. As a result, `<ci>x</ci>` and `<ci> x </ci>` produce two different `math:FreeVariableDeclaration` nodes. In `x + x`, one variable then becomes two distinct variables.

MathML token content ignores leading and trailing whitespace. Use the trimmed value for the identity.

